# Input graph for RDFLib__prez__tests_test_endpoints_spaceprez.py__test_feature -- written during translation.
#
# The region checks that ONE exact, fully-bound triple is present in the
# response graph -- `next(response_graph.triples((Feature1, RDF.type,
# GEO.Feature)))`, no variable is ever bound. Since the pattern has no free
# term, "several solutions" does not apply the same way it would for a
# selecting query; what this fixture DOES cover:
#
#   * the exact triple under test (Feature1 a geo:Feature);
#   * NEIGHBOURHOOD that must NOT satisfy it: a second feature (Feature2,
#     also geo:Feature, wrong subject) and a second type on Feature1 itself
#     (dcat:Dataset, wrong object) -- if the match were accidentally
#     type-only or subject-only, one of these would make it pass regardless.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix geo: <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .

<https://example.com/spaceprez/Feature1> a geo:Feature ;
    dcat:title "Feature One" .

<https://example.com/spaceprez/Feature2> a geo:Feature .
<https://example.com/spaceprez/Feature1> a dcat:Dataset .
